			"id":"5e5082c03b2b1a06",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"IELTS WRITING TASK 2 — MASTER WORKBOOK\n\n**Từ ý tưởng đến bài luận có lập luận | Dành cho học viên Việt Nam hướng tới Band 6.5–7.5**  \n**Student Workbook + Teacher’s Answer Key**\n\n**Thông điệp chính:** _Depth > Quantity._ Viết một ý rõ, giải thích được **vì sao** và **bằng cách nào**, rồi chỉ ra kết quả đáng quan tâm. Không học thuộc bài mẫu hay cố nhồi từ khó.\n\n**Thông tin lớp học**  \nHọ tên: …………………………………………………. Lớp: …………………… Ngày: ……………………\n\n## Hướng dẫn sử dụng\n\n•           **Quy tắc học:** Knowledge / Insight → Applying Exercise → Sentence Building → Argument Building → Paragraph Building → Full Essay Application.\n\n•           **Khi làm bài:** Che phần **18. Answer Key**. Trả lời vào vở hoặc ngay dưới từng hoạt động. Các bài mẫu chỉ là _suggested answers_; mọi cách lập luận hợp lý, đúng đề đều có thể chấp nhận.\n\n•           **Lộ trình gợi ý (8 buổi, 90 phút/buổi):** Buổi 1: mục 1–3; buổi 2: mục 4–5.4; buổi 3: mục 5.5–7; buổi 4: mục 8–10; buổi 5: mục 11–13; buổi 6: mục 14–15; buổi 7: mục 16; buổi 8: mục 17 + sửa bài.\n\n•           **Chuẩn bài thi:** IELTS Writing Task 2 tối thiểu 250 từ, thời lượng khuyến nghị khoảng 40 phút; Task 2 có trọng số gấp đôi Task 1 trong Writing. Bốn tiêu chí chấm điểm có trọng số bằng nhau trong mỗi task. Các mô tả band trong tài liệu này là diễn giải giảng dạy, **không phải cam kết mức điểm**.\n\n**Bản đồ kỹ năng:** Đọc đúng câu hỏi → Xác định lập trường → Chọn 2 ý mạnh → Giải thích WHY/HOW → Dẫn đến RESULT → Minh họa có mục đích → Đánh giá WHY IT MATTERS → Ghép thành đoạn → Kiểm tra toàn bài.\n\n## MỤC LỤC — 18 CHUYÊN ĐỀ\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|01  Understanding Task 2|10  Writing conclusions|\n|02  Twelve question types|11  Coherence and cohesion|\n|03  Four-step question analysis|12  Grammar toolkit|\n|04  From idea to argument|13  Hedging and academic caution|\n|05  Essential sentence functions|14  Natural language bank|\n|06  Deepening one argument|15  Common learner errors|\n|07  Building a body paragraph|16  Twelve guided mini tasks|\n|08  Writing introductions|17  Full essay application|\n|09  Thesis and clear position|18  Teacher’s answer key|\n\n# 1. UNDERSTANDING IELTS WRITING TASK 2\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nWriting Task 2 không đo khả năng thuộc câu mở bài. Bài thi đánh giá bạn có **trả lời chính xác câu hỏi**, triển khai ý có cơ sở, tổ chức mạch lạc và sử dụng tiếng Anh phù hợp hay không.\n\n|**Tiêu chí**|**Examiner quan sát**|**Band 6 — biểu hiện thường gặp**|**Band 7 — tiến bộ nổi bật**|**Band 8 — khả năng kiểm soát cao hơn**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|**Task Response (TR)**|Trả lời mọi phần của đề, lập trường, ý chính được giải thích và hỗ trợ|Trả lời được nhưng có ý phát triển chưa đầy đủ hoặc chưa liên quan hoàn toàn|Lập trường rõ xuyên suốt; ý chính phù hợp và được phát triển, hỗ trợ|Trả lời đủ, cân nhắc thuyết phục và phát triển ý sâu, chính xác hơn|\n|**Coherence & Cohesion (CC)**|Mạch lập luận, bố cục, tham chiếu và liên kết câu|Có trình tự nhưng đôi lúc nối câu máy móc hoặc tham chiếu thiếu rõ|Tiến triển hợp lý, mỗi đoạn có trọng tâm, liên kết linh hoạt|Dẫn dắt rất trôi chảy, quan hệ giữa các ý tự nhiên và rõ|\n|**Lexical Resource (LR)**|Dùng từ đúng nghĩa, đúng ngữ cảnh, đúng collocation|Đủ từ để diễn đạt nhưng đôi khi sai kết hợp từ/lặp từ|Dùng từ linh hoạt và chính xác hơn, có một số cách diễn đạt ít gặp nhưng phù hợp|Phạm vi từ và mức chính xác cao, lựa chọn sắc thái tự nhiên|\n|**Grammatical Range & Accuracy (GRA)**|Cấu trúc đa dạng, độ chính xác, dấu câu|Có câu đơn và phức; lỗi đôi khi ảnh hưởng chất lượng|Dùng linh hoạt nhiều cấu trúc, thường tạo câu ít lỗi|Phần lớn câu được kiểm soát tốt, lỗi hiếm hoặc không đáng kể|\n\n**Lỗi thường gặp của học viên Việt Nam:** TR — nêu 4–5 ý nhưng không giải thích; CC — câu nào cũng _Furthermore/Moreover_; LR — dịch từng chữ (_make pollution_, _very convenience_); GRA — nhiều mệnh đề ghép không có chủ ngữ/động từ hoàn chỉnh.\n\n**Sửa theo ưu tiên:** (1) đúng task và lập trường → (2) mỗi đoạn có một ý đủ sâu → (3) ngắt câu kiểm soát → (4) thay từ thiếu tự nhiên → (5) kiểm tra lỗi ngữ pháp phổ biến.\n\n**Having an idea ≠ developing an argument**\n\n|**Mức**|**Ví dụ**|**Vấn đề/giá trị**|\n|---|---|---|\n|Idea|Technology is useful.|Chủ đề quá chung|\n|Claim|Technology can improve access to education.|Biết rõ lợi ích nào|\n|Explanation|Students in remote areas may struggle to find qualified teachers.|Giải thích nhu cầu thực tế|\n|Mechanism|Online lessons allow them to study with teachers outside their local communities.|Chỉ ra điều gì tạo ra lợi ích|\n|Consequence|This can reduce differences in learning opportunities.|Nêu kết quả|\n|Example|A rural student can attend a live mathematics lesson without travelling to a city.|Minh họa cơ chế|\n|Evaluation|The benefit matters most where local educational resources are limited.|Làm rõ ý nghĩa, phạm vi|\n\n**Chuỗi tư duy:** Idea → Claim → Explanation → Mechanism → Consequence → Example → Evaluation. Không nhất thiết viết đủ bảy câu; phải hiểu đủ bảy chức năng.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E01\n\nVới mỗi ý dưới đây, hãy viết **Claim → WHY → HOW → RESULT → EXAMPLE → WHY IT MATTERS** (mỗi ô 5–20 từ tiếng Anh). Không được lặp nguyên câu trước.\n\n1.          Public transport is good.\n\n2.          Working from home is convenient.\n\n3.          Exams are stressful.\n\n**Tự chấm:** Claim có cụ thể không? WHY bổ sung lý do? HOW có bước trung gian? Example chứng minh được ý vừa nêu? Evaluation có trả lời câu hỏi _So what?_\n\n# 2. UNDERSTANDING THE 12 TASK 2 QUESTION TYPES\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n**Lưu ý quan trọng:** 12 loại dưới đây là **nhóm đề phục vụ học tập**, không phải 12 hạng mục chấm chính thức. Hai cách diễn đạt _Do you agree or disagree?_ và _To what extent do you agree or disagree?_ thường được xử lý bằng cùng năng lực nêu mức độ đồng tình. Một số đề yêu cầu opinion dù không dùng chữ _opinion_.\n\n**Ký hiệu bố cục:** I = Introduction, B1 = Body 1, B2 = Body 2, C = Conclusion. Cấu trúc 4 đoạn là lựa chọn an toàn thường dùng, không phải luật bắt buộc. Bài trả lời phải phù hợp nội dung đề hơn là phù hợp một khuôn.\n\n### 2.1 Agree / Disagree\n\n**Nhận diện:** _Do you agree or disagree?_ **Bắt buộc:** chọn và bảo vệ lập trường đối với nhận định. **Tùy chọn:** có thể nhắc lập luận phía kia nếu giúp lý giải; không buộc cân đều hai bên. **Opinion:** bắt buộc, nêu ở I và giữ nhất quán ở B1/B2/C.\n\n**Bố cục hợp lý:** I — paraphrase + opinion; B1 — lý do 1; B2 — lý do 2 hoặc giải quyết phản biện; C — khẳng định lại lập trường. **Tránh:** viết B1 ủng hộ, B2 phản đối mà không cho biết cuối cùng đồng ý hay không.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Governments should make public transport free for everyone. Do you agree or disagree?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _University education should focus only on subjects that help students find jobs. Do you agree or disagree?_\n\n**E02.1:** Gạch keyword trong A. Viết: task = …; opinion required = …; thesis 1 câu = …; B1 = …; B2 = … .\n\n### 2.2 To What Extent Do You Agree or Disagree?\n\n**Nhận diện:** _To what extent…?_ **Bắt buộc:** nêu rõ mức độ (_completely / largely / partly / disagree_) và bảo vệ đúng mức đó. **Tùy chọn:** partial agreement; không bắt buộc chọn 50/50. **Opinion:** ở I, làm rõ trong từng B.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — mức độ đồng tình; B1 — phần đồng tình mạnh; B2 — giới hạn/điều kiện hoặc lý do bổ sung; C — kết luận theo cùng mức độ. **Tránh:** _I partly agree_ nhưng hai đoạn không thể hiện điều kiện/ràng buộc.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _The main purpose of education is to prepare people for employment. To what extent do you agree or disagree?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Children should spend less time using digital devices. To what extent do you agree or disagree?_\n\n**E02.2:** Với A, chọn mức độ đồng tình, ghi giới hạn của lập trường và viết thesis 1 câu.\n\n### 2.3 Discuss Both Views\n\n**Nhận diện:** _Discuss both views._ **Bắt buộc:** giải thích đúng và đủ **hai quan điểm**, không biến thành ưu/nhược của một lựa chọn. **Opinion:** không được yêu cầu trực tiếp; có thể tránh đưa vào để dành dung lượng phân tích cả hai bên.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — giới thiệu tranh luận; B1 — logic quan điểm 1; B2 — logic quan điểm 2; C — tổng hợp hai lý do trọng tâm. **Tránh:** thêm lập trường cá nhân chiếm nhiều dung lượng khiến một quan điểm bị bỏ quên.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Some people believe children learn best at home, while others believe they learn best at school. Discuss both views._  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Some people prefer living in cities, while others prefer rural areas. Discuss both views._\n\n**E02.3:** Với A, ghi từng quan điểm thành **một câu claim riêng**, kèm WHY; không viết “advantages and disadvantages” chung chung.\n\n### 2.4 Discuss Both Views AND Give Your Opinion\n\n**Nhận diện:** có đúng cụm _and give your own opinion_. **Bắt buộc:** trình bày hai views **và** quan điểm của mình. **Opinion:** nêu ở I, củng cố trong B2 hoặc sau khi so sánh, nhắc lại ở C.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — cả hai views + opinion; B1 — view 1; B2 — view 2 + vì sao mình chọn view này (hoặc nêu đánh giá cân nhắc rõ); C — chốt. **Tránh:** discuss cả hai nhưng không có câu trả lời của bản thân.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Some people think schools should ban smartphones, while others believe they can be useful learning tools. Discuss both views and give your opinion._  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Some believe cities should invest in roads, while others favour public transport. Discuss both views and give your opinion._\n\n**E02.4:** Với A, viết 1 câu WHY cho mỗi view rồi thesis có opinion.\n\n### 2.5 Advantages and Disadvantages\n\n**Nhận diện:** _What are the advantages and disadvantages?_ **Bắt buộc:** trình bày cả mặt lợi và bất lợi, không bỏ sót. **Opinion:** không bắt buộc so sánh mặt nào thắng nếu đề chỉ hỏi liệt kê và phân tích hai mặt.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — xác định xu hướng; B1 — một lợi ích có giải thích; B2 — một hạn chế có giải thích; C — tổng hợp. **Tránh:** khẳng định _benefits outweigh drawbacks_ mà không chứng minh khi không được hỏi.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _What are the advantages and disadvantages of working remotely?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _What are the advantages and disadvantages of living in a large city?_\n\n**E02.5:** Với A, viết 1 benefit + HOW và 1 drawback + HOW; phân biệt hai cơ chế.\n\n### 2.6 Do the Advantages Outweigh the Disadvantages?\n\n**Nhận diện:** _Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?_ **Bắt buộc:** phân tích hai mặt **và đánh giá mặt nào lớn hơn**. **Opinion:** bắt buộc từ I đến C.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — phán đoán; B1 — mặt yếu hơn (giải thích thực chất); B2 — mặt mạnh hơn + tiêu chí so sánh (quy mô, thời gian, số người hưởng lợi); C — khẳng định cân nhắc. **Tránh:** hai đoạn lợi/hại nhưng không có phép cân.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _More people are buying goods online rather than in shops. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Many employees now use AI assistants at work. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?_\n\n**E02.6:** Với A, nêu **tiêu chí so sánh** và thesis thể hiện bên nào thắng.\n\n### 2.7 Problems and Solutions\n\n**Nhận diện:** _What problems does this cause and how can they be solved?_ **Bắt buộc:** hậu quả tiêu cực và biện pháp xử lý từng vấn đề. **Opinion:** không buộc đưa lập trường đồng ý/phản đối; phải đánh giá tính phù hợp của giải pháp.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — khái quát vấn đề; B1 — 1–2 problem có cơ chế; B2 — giải pháp **khớp trực tiếp** từng vấn đề; C — kết quả kỳ vọng. **Tránh:** viết nguyên nhân khi đề hỏi vấn đề, hoặc giải pháp không liên quan.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Many cities face serious traffic congestion. What problems does this cause, and what solutions can be introduced?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _A growing number of young people have poor sleep habits. What problems can this cause, and how can they be addressed?_\n\n**E02.7:** Với A, nối _Problem → Measure → HOW measure works_ bằng ba dòng.\n\n### 2.8 Causes and Solutions\n\n**Nhận diện:** _What are the causes and what measures could address this?_ **Bắt buộc:** lý do xảy ra + cách can thiệp vào nguyên nhân. **Opinion:** không buộc chọn phe, có thể đánh giá biện pháp khả thi.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — vấn đề; B1 — 1–2 nguyên nhân; B2 — giải pháp nhắm vào nguyên nhân; C — chốt. **Tránh:** nhầm _cause_ (vì sao xảy ra) với _effect_ (điều gì xảy ra tiếp).\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Obesity rates are rising in many countries. What are the main causes, and what can be done to address them?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _More students are choosing not to study science. What causes this, and how could the trend be reversed?_\n\n**E02.8:** Với B, ghi Cause = …; Evidence/Mechanism = …; Targeted solution = … .\n\n### 2.9 Causes and Effects\n\n**Nhận diện:** _What are the causes and effects?_ **Bắt buộc:** vì sao hiện tượng hình thành và hệ quả. **Opinion:** không bắt buộc. **Solution:** không bắt buộc; nếu đề không hỏi, đừng dành cả đoạn cho giải pháp.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — hiện tượng; B1 — nguyên nhân chính; B2 — hệ quả được giải thích; C — tổng hợp quan hệ nguyên nhân → tác động.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _In many countries, fewer people are reading books for pleasure. What are the causes and effects of this trend?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Young adults are increasingly delaying marriage. What are the causes and effects of this development?_\n\n**E02.9:** Với A, viết một **cause** rồi đi qua **mechanism** đến một **effect**, không thêm solution.\n\n### 2.10 Two-Part / Direct Questions\n\n**Nhận diện:** hai câu hỏi riêng, ví dụ _Why…? Is this…?_ **Bắt buộc:** trả lời **cả hai**. **Opinion:** phụ thuộc câu hỏi 2 (nếu “Is this positive?” thì có).\n\n**Bố cục:** I — trả lời ngắn cả hai câu; B1 — câu hỏi 1; B2 — câu hỏi 2; C — tóm tắt hai kết luận. **Tránh:** dành quá nhiều cho câu 1 rồi bỏ câu 2.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _More people are choosing to live alone. Why is this happening? Is it a positive or negative development?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Many young people change jobs frequently. Why does this happen? What are the consequences?_\n\n**E02.10:** Với A, tách hai câu hỏi, viết **hai phần câu trả lời** trong cùng một thesis.\n\n### 2.11 Positive or Negative Development\n\n**Nhận diện:** _Is this a positive or negative development?_ **Bắt buộc:** đánh giá xu hướng là tích cực/tiêu cực (hoặc tích cực với điều kiện rõ ràng). **Opinion:** bắt buộc.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — đánh giá; B1 — tác động quan trọng 1; B2 — tác động quan trọng 2 hoặc xử lý một hạn chế; C — cân nhắc cuối. **Tránh:** chỉ mô tả xu hướng hoặc liệt kê pros/cons không kết luận.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _More people are paying for goods using mobile phones rather than cash. Is this a positive or negative development?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _Increasing numbers of people prefer online courses to face-to-face classes. Is this a positive or negative development?_\n\n**E02.11:** Với B, viết một thesis có điều kiện (_provided that…_) và hai ý hỗ trợ.\n\n### 2.12 Mixed / Hybrid Questions\n\n**Nhận diện:** hai yêu cầu **khác loại** trong cùng đề, ví dụ _causes + opinion_ hoặc _both views + solutions_. **Bắt buộc:** bóc tách chính xác từng động từ yêu cầu. **Opinion:** tùy câu hỏi, nhưng nếu có _Do you agree/Is this good?_ thì bắt buộc.\n\n**Bố cục:** I — trả lời hai yêu cầu; B1 — yêu cầu 1; B2 — yêu cầu 2; C — kết luận phù hợp. **Tránh:** chọn sai một khuôn vì chỉ nhìn một keyword.\n\n**Ví dụ A:** _Why are private vehicles becoming more popular, and do you think governments should discourage their use?_  \n**Ví dụ B:** _What problems are caused by fast fashion, and who should be responsible for addressing them?_\n\n**E02.12:** Với B, gạch 2 task, chọn phạm vi giải pháp/trách nhiệm và viết thesis hai vế.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E02 MASTER CHECK\n\n**Nhiệm vụ:** Đối với cả 12 câu A ở trên, đánh dấu keywords; ghi **required response / opinion required? / 4-paragraph map**. Sau đó viết **một thesis** cho 2.1, 2.4, 2.6, 2.10, 2.12.\n\n**So sánh dễ nhầm:**\n\n|**Cặp đề**|**Khác nhau nằm ở đâu?**|\n|---|---|\n|Discuss both views / …and give your opinion|Loại thứ hai bắt buộc thể hiện và duy trì opinion; loại đầu tập trung giải thích cả hai views|\n|Advantages & disadvantages / Do advantages outweigh…|Loại sau yêu cầu **weighing** — tiêu chí so sánh và kết luận mặt nào vượt trội|\n|Do you agree… / To what extent…|Cả hai đều cần stance; _extent_ nhấn mạnh mức độ rõ, không buộc “partly agree”|\n|Problems / Causes|_Problem_ là điều gây hại; _cause_ là yếu tố tạo ra hiện tượng|\n\n# 3. A FOUR-STEP QUESTION ANALYSIS\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n1.          **Topic:** Lĩnh vực rộng đang nói đến là gì? (_technology in education_).\n\n2.          **Task:** Người ra đề yêu cầu hành động nào? (_evaluate whether advantages outweigh disadvantages_).\n\n3.          **Scope:** Khía cạnh cần bàn chính xác là gì? (_using AI tools in classrooms_, không phải mọi công nghệ).\n\n4.          **Position:** Câu trả lời cốt lõi của mình là gì? (_advantages are greater when use is supervised_).\n\nĐặt bốn thành phần thành một câu: **Although [counterpoint], [position] because [main reason].** Chỉ dùng khi phù hợp với loại đề.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E03\n\nĐiền Topic / Task / Scope / Position cho 5 đề. Có thể chọn lập trường khác nếu giải thích hợp lý.\n\n1.          _Some people believe schools should teach financial literacy. To what extent do you agree or disagree?_\n\n2.          _Many companies are allowing employees to work from home. What are the advantages and disadvantages?_\n\n3.          _In some cities, cycling is becoming more popular. Why is this happening? Is it a positive development?_\n\n4.          _Some people believe teenagers should do volunteer work, while others think they should focus on schoolwork. Discuss both views and give your opinion._\n\n5.          _Plastic waste is increasing in many countries. What causes this, and how can the problem be addressed?_\n\n**Mẫu ghi:** Topic: ______ | Task: ______ | Scope: ______ | Position: ______\n\n# 4. FROM IDEA TO ARGUMENT — THE ARGUMENT LADDER\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n|**Bước**|**Câu hỏi giáo viên đặt**|**Chức năng trong bài**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**WHAT?**|Chính xác em khẳng định điều gì?|Claim rõ, có giới hạn|\n|**WHY?**|Điều gì khiến claim hợp lý?|Lý do, điều kiện ban đầu|\n|**HOW?**|Cơ chế trung gian nào nối nguyên nhân với kết quả?|Lập luận có tính giải thích|\n|**RESULT?**|Hệ quả trực tiếp nào xuất hiện?|Chứng minh vì sao claim đáng bàn|\n|**EXAMPLE?**|Một trường hợp giả định cụ thể nào minh họa đúng cơ chế?|Hình dung được, không bịa dữ liệu|\n|**WHY IT MATTERS?**|Hệ quả có ý nghĩa với ai, về lâu dài ra sao?|Đánh giá, kết nối lại đề|\n\n**Worked example — social media**\n\n•           **WHAT:** Excessive social media use can harm some teenagers’ mental well-being.\n\n•           **WHY:** Their feeds often contain idealised images of other people’s lives.\n\n•           **HOW:** Repeated exposure may encourage comparisons with unrealistic standards.\n\n•           **RESULT:** Such comparisons can undermine self-esteem and increase dissatisfaction over time.\n\n•           **EXAMPLE:** A teenager comparing their appearance with heavily edited photos may become more critical of their own body.\n\n•           **WHY IT MATTERS:** This risk is particularly important during adolescence, when confidence and identity are still developing.\n\n**Đoạn ghép tự nhiên:** _Excessive social media use can undermine some teenagers’ mental well-being because their feeds often contain idealised images of other people’s lives. Repeated exposure may encourage comparisons with unrealistic standards, gradually reducing self-esteem. For example, a teenager who frequently compares their appearance with edited photographs may develop an overly critical view of their body. This is particularly concerning during adolescence, when confidence and identity are still developing._\n\n**Phân biệt:** “Social media is bad. For example, teenagers use Instagram. It also wastes time.” chỉ đặt ba nhận xét cạnh nhau, không tạo chuỗi WHY → HOW.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E04\n\nViết 4 chuỗi. Mỗi dòng cần **Claim, WHY, HOW, Immediate Result, Long-term Result, Example, Why It Matters**. Gợi ý không nhất thiết dùng hết trong đoạn cuối.\n\n1.          _Free public libraries benefit local communities._\n\n2.          _Long commuting times can affect employees’ well-being._\n\n3.          _School uniforms may reduce visible economic differences._\n\n4.          _Excessive reliance on AI may weaken independent learning._\n\n**Peer review:** Bạn học đọc chain và đánh dấu **MISSING LINK** nếu từ A nhảy thẳng đến B mà thiếu HOW.\n\n# 5. ESSENTIAL SENTENCE FUNCTIONS\n\n**Nguyên tắc:** Mỗi mẫu câu dưới đây là **công cụ để diễn đạt quan hệ logic**, không phải câu bắt buộc phải xuất hiện. Tất cả ví dụ tiếng Anh cần đọc hiểu và biến đổi được.\n\n## 5.1 Claim — nêu luận điểm\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Claim phải đưa ra một nội dung **có thể giải thích hoặc bảo vệ**, không chỉ lặp lại chủ đề. **Function:** định hướng đoạn.\n\n**Reusable frameworks:** _A key reason why X occurs is that…_; _One significant consequence of X is…_; _One particularly important benefit of X is…_\n\n**Model:** _One major benefit of public transport is that it makes essential services more accessible to people who cannot drive._\n\n**Common mistake:** _Technology has many benefits._ (mơ hồ). **E05.1:** Viết lại _Education is important_ và _Cities have problems_ thành hai claims cụ thể.\n\n## 5.2 Explanation — trả lời WHY\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Giải thích phải bổ sung thông tin; lặp lại claim bằng từ khác không được tính là phát triển. **Function:** làm rõ vì sao hiện tượng xảy ra.\n\n**Frameworks:** _This is largely because…_; _The main reason for this is that…_; _One explanation is that…_\n\n**Wrong:** _Students cheat because they are under pressure. This is because they feel pressured._\n\n**Model:** _Some students cheat because admission decisions depend heavily on a small number of examinations._\n\n**E05.2:** Bổ sung WHY có thông tin mới cho _Public libraries matter to low-income families._\n\n## 5.3 Cause — nguyên nhân\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** _lead to/result in_ nhấn hệ quả; _contribute to_ diễn tả một yếu tố góp phần; _stem from/be driven by_ nhìn ngược về nguồn gốc. **Function:** thiết lập quan hệ nhân quả có mức độ phù hợp.\n\n**Frameworks:** _X can lead to Y_; _X may contribute to Y_; _X may partly stem from Y_; _X is often driven by Y_.\n\n**Model:** _High housing costs can contribute to longer commuting times as workers move farther from city centres._\n\n**Mistake:** _Traffic causes all air pollution._ (quá tuyệt đối). **E05.3:** Ghép _poor public transport / increased car use / congestion_ thành hai câu nhân quả.\n\n## 5.4 Mechanism — giải thích HOW\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** **Cause ≠ mechanism.** “Academic pressure causes cheating” thiếu bước ở giữa. Đặt câu hỏi: _Khi người đó bị áp lực, họ suy nghĩ/hành động gì khiến gian lận xảy ra?_\n\n**Logic:** A (pressure) → **X (fear of failure and perceived need to protect exam results)** → B (cheating).\n\n**Frameworks:** _When…_; _By + V-ing…_; _Through…_; _This often happens when…_; _In situations where…_\n\n**Model:** _When students believe that a single examination will determine their future, some may see cheating as a way to avoid failure._\n\n**Mistake:** _By students study online, they save time._ → _By studying online, students can save commuting time._\n\n**E05.4:** Điền cơ chế: _Expensive housing → [HOW workers respond] → longer commutes_; _Regular reading → [HOW language develops] → stronger vocabulary_.\n\n## 5.5 Consequence — hệ quả\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Hãy đi từ **immediate → secondary → long-term**, nhưng không phóng đại kết quả chắc chắn. **Function:** cho thấy chuỗi tác động.\n\n**Frameworks:** _As a result,…_; _This can in turn lead to…_; _Over the longer term,…_; _The immediate consequence is that…_\n\n**Model:** _Long commutes reduce time available for rest. This can in turn increase fatigue and, over time, affect job satisfaction._\n\n**Mistake:** _As a result… Consequently… Therefore…_ liên tiếp không có ý mới. **E05.5:** Tiếp tục hai mức hệ quả cho _If cities become less walkable, residents may rely more heavily on cars._\n\n## 5.6 Example — minh họa\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Example phải **thể hiện claim + mechanism**, không thay thế explanation. Có thể dùng tình huống hợp lý giả định, không tự nhận là số liệu thật.\n\n**Frameworks:** _For example,…_; _Consider, for example,…_; _This can be illustrated by…_\n\n**Weak:** _For example, many students cheat._\n\n**Model:** _For example, a student using an AI tool secretly during a take-home examination may receive a high mark without understanding the material._\n\n**E05.6:** Cải thiện _For example, people use public transport_ thành ví dụ có người, hành động, kết quả.\n\n## 5.7 Conditional — lập luận có điều kiện\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Conditional cho thấy **điều kiện → kết quả có thể xảy ra**, hữu ích khi đánh giá giải pháp. **Function:** tránh khẳng định thiếu điều kiện.\n\n**Frameworks:** _If X happens, Y may…_; _Unless X is addressed, Y may…_; _Without X, Y is likely to…_; _If X were…, Y might…_\n\n**Model:** _Unless affordable housing is available near employment centres, many workers may continue to face long commutes._\n\n**Mistake:** _If governments will invest, traffic will reduce._ → _If governments invest in reliable buses, car use may fall._\n\n**E05.7:** Hoàn thành _Without clear rules on AI use, students may…_ và _If employers offered flexible hours, …_\n\n## 5.8 Comparison — so sánh để lập luận\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** So sánh **theo cùng tiêu chí**: cost, accessibility, long-term impact… **Function:** cân nhắc lựa chọn.\n\n**Frameworks:** _Compared with…_; _Whereas…_; _X is more likely to… than Y_; _X has a greater impact on… than Y_.\n\n**Model:** _Compared with building more roads, improving bus services may help a wider range of residents at a lower individual cost._\n\n**Mistake:** _Online education is better than schools._ (khác tiêu chí). **E05.8:** So sánh online và in-person learning theo _flexibility_, không tuyên bố bên nào hơn về mọi mặt.\n\n## 5.9 Contrast — chỉ ra khác biệt\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Contrast đặt hai sự thật khác nhau cạnh nhau; **concession** còn công nhận một điểm của bên khác rồi phản hồi nó. **Function:** làm rõ khác biệt.\n\n**Frameworks:** _While…_; _Whereas…_; _However,…_; _In contrast,…_\n\n**Model:** _While online courses allow flexible schedules, classroom lessons provide more opportunities for immediate feedback._\n\n**Mistake:** _Although online courses are flexible, but…_ → chỉ dùng một trong hai. **E05.9:** Viết 1 câu contrast về city vs rural living.\n\n## 5.10 Concession — công nhận và giới hạn phản biện\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** **Accept → Limit → Respond**; không tạo “both sides” vô định. **Function:** tăng độ cân bằng và sức thuyết phục.\n\n**Frameworks:** _Admittedly,…_; _There is some merit in the argument that…_; _Although it is true that…_\n\n**Model:** _Admittedly, strict punishment may discourage some students from cheating. However, punishment alone is unlikely to address the academic pressure that contributes to this behaviour._\n\n**Mistake:** _Both opinions are good._ (không đánh giá). **E05.10:** Viết cặp concession + response về _banning smartphones at school_.\n\n## 5.11 Counterargument — phản biện có căn cứ\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Không nói phía kia “completely wrong” nếu chưa chứng minh. **Function:** chỉ ra yếu tố bị bỏ sót.\n\n**Frameworks:** _However, this overlooks the fact that…_; _This argument is limited because…_; _Focusing solely on X would be too narrow an approach._\n\n**Model:** _Banning all digital devices may reduce distractions, but this overlooks their potential value for students with limited access to learning materials._\n\n**Mistake:** _This opinion is nonsense._ (cảm tính). **E05.11:** Phản biện _All homework should be removed because children need rest_ bằng một giới hạn có lý.\n\n## 5.12 Evaluation — trả lời SO WHAT?\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** Evaluation nói **vì sao hệ quả quan trọng**, với nhóm người nào, trong hoàn cảnh nào. **Function:** khép lại lập luận thay vì đột ngột chuyển ý.\n\n**Frameworks:** _This is particularly important because…_; _This is especially concerning because…_; _The wider significance is that…_; _For this reason,…_\n\n**Model:** _This is particularly important for low-income households, which may not have the resources to pay for private tutoring._\n\n**Mistake:** _This is a very big problem._ (không nói “big” ở điểm nào). **E05.12:** Thêm evaluation cho _Long commutes can reduce the time parents spend with their children._\n\n## 5.13 Solution / Recommendation — giải pháp có cơ chế\n\n**Knowledge / Insight:** **Problem → Measure → Mechanism → Expected Result.** Nêu ai thực hiện và làm sao biện pháp chạm vào nguyên nhân. **Function:** chuyển từ mô tả đến hành động khả thi.\n\n**Frameworks:** _One practical measure would be to…_; _A more effective approach would be to…_; _Rather than relying solely on X, governments could…_; _X should complement rather than replace Y._\n\n**Model:** _Rather than banning phones completely, schools could restrict their use during independent work while allowing supervised activities that require digital resources._\n\n**Mistake:** _The government should solve this problem by raising awareness._ (chung chung). **E05.13:** Phát triển _Cities should reduce traffic_ thành giải pháp cụ thể gồm owner, measure, HOW và expected result.\n\n# 6. DEEPENING ONE ARGUMENT\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n**Weak:** Idea 1 → Idea 2 → Idea 3 → Idea 4 (mỗi ý một câu, không phát triển).  \n**Strong:** One relevant idea → WHY → HOW → immediate result → further result → (example if helpful) → evaluation.\n\nMột lập luận có thể lan qua nhiều mức **Individual → Family → School/Workplace → Organisation → Society → Economy → Long term**. Chỉ chọn mức thực sự giải thích đề; không cố dẫn mọi ý đến GDP hoặc toàn xã hội.\n\n**Worked chain — remote work:** _Remote workers avoid daily commuting → save travel time → gain more time for rest or family → experience better work-life balance → may report higher job satisfaction._\n\n**Paragraph (không nhồi tất cả các mức):** _One important benefit of remote work is the time employees save by avoiding daily commutes. In large cities, travelling to and from the office can take several hours, leaving less time for family or rest. By working from home, employees can use some of that time for personal responsibilities, which may improve their work-life balance. Over time, this may also support job satisfaction, particularly among workers with long journeys._\n\n## Applying Exercise — E06\n\nChọn **một** ý trong bốn ý sau và viết đoạn 4–6 câu. Nêu 1 WHY, 1 HOW, ít nhất 1 RESULT và 1 EVALUATION.\n\n1.          _Public parks improve urban life._\n\n2.          _Part-time jobs can benefit university students._\n\n3.          _Online shopping can disadvantage local shops._\n\n4.          _Early financial education can help young adults._\n\n**Teacher check:** Highlight claim (xanh), WHY (vàng), HOW (hồng), RESULT (cam), evaluation (gạch chân). Nếu không tìm thấy HOW, viết lại.\n\n# 7. BUILDING A STRONG BODY PARAGRAPH\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n**Thinking framework — không phải khuôn 6 câu:** (1) Main claim → (2) explanation → (3) mechanism → (4) consequence → (5) example nếu cần → (6) evaluation/link. Một câu có thể phục vụ nhiều chức năng. _Không bắt buộc_ câu nào cũng bắt đầu bằng connector.\n\n**Weak paragraph — minh họa những yếu tố thường hạn chế điểm:**\n\n_Online learning is very good. Firstly, it is convenient. Secondly, it is cheap. Moreover, students can study. For example, there are many online classes. Therefore, online learning is very important._\n\n**Vì sao yếu:** vague claim; không có WHY/HOW; lặp “good/important”; example quá chung; linking words chỉ nối các nhận xét rời rạc.\n\n**Improved paragraph — bước trung gian:**\n\n_Online learning can make education more convenient for students who live far from school. They can attend lessons from home, so they do not need to spend time travelling. For example, students in rural communities may join online classes with teachers from another region. This can help more students access education._\n\n**Đã tốt hơn:** một lợi ích rõ, cơ chế giảm di chuyển, ví dụ đúng. **Chưa tối ưu:** “convenient” và “access education” còn rộng; chiều sâu về đối tượng chưa đầy đủ.\n\n**More developed paragraph — định hướng Band 7+:**\n\n_One significant benefit of online learning is that it can widen access to education for students living in remote areas. These students may have few specialist teachers nearby, making it difficult to study certain subjects in depth. Through live lessons and recorded materials, they can learn from qualified teachers without relocating or travelling long distances. For example, a student in a rural community could attend an advanced mathematics class that is not offered at their local school. This flexibility matters because educational opportunities should not depend entirely on where a student lives._\n\n**Vì sao hiệu quả:** claim đúng trọng tâm; giải thích **điều kiện ban đầu**; HOW diễn tả cách tiếp cận tài nguyên; ví dụ gắn với “specialist teachers”; đánh giá nối về **equity**, không phóng đại “everyone”. “Band 7+” ở đây là **định hướng kỹ thuật viết**, không phải mức điểm giám khảo chính thức cho đoạn đứng riêng.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E07\n\n**Topic:** _Working remotely can benefit employees._  \n**Step 1** Claim cụ thể = __________________.  \n**Step 2** Explanation (WHY) = __________________.  \n**Step 3** Mechanism (HOW) = __________________.  \n**Step 4** Result = __________________.  \n**Step 5** Example **hoặc** evaluation = __________________.  \n**Step 6** Ghép thành **một** body paragraph 90–115 từ (không cần 6 câu chính xác).\n\n**Checklist:** một claim; không lặp claim bằng synonym; nối cause–effect hợp lý; ví dụ minh họa chứ không thay WHY; sử dụng pronouns rõ đối tượng.\n\n# 8. INTRODUCTIONS THAT ANSWER THE QUESTION\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nMột introduction hiệu quả thường chỉ cần **(1) meaning-based paraphrase of the issue + (2) thesis answering the task**. Có thể thêm roadmap nếu thực sự giúp định hướng, không bắt buộc. **Paraphrase ≠ thay từng từ bằng synonym**; hãy giữ đúng quan hệ và mức độ của nhận định gốc.\n\n**Weak:** _In today’s modern era, technology is a controversial issue. This essay will discuss both sides and give my opinion._  \n**Better:** _Although digital tools can distract students, I believe their educational benefits are greater when their use is carefully supervised._\n\n|**Dạng đề**|**Natural thesis / introduction move (không học thuộc nguyên câu)**|\n|---|---|\n|Agree / Disagree|_I believe this policy would be beneficial because it could improve access to essential services._|\n|To what extent|_I largely agree, although the benefits may depend on how the policy is implemented._|\n|Discuss both views|_The debate centres on whether formal schooling or home-based learning provides a more suitable environment for children._|\n|Both views + opinion|_While both approaches have strengths, I favour classroom learning because it offers more consistent social interaction and support._|\n|Advantages / Disadvantages|_Remote work offers greater flexibility, but it can also make collaboration more difficult._|\n|Outweigh|_Despite some concerns about quality, I believe the accessibility of online learning makes its benefits more significant overall._|\n|Problems / Solutions|_Traffic congestion can undermine public health and productivity, but better public transport and urban planning could reduce these effects._|\n|Two-part|_This trend is largely driven by housing costs, and I consider it a negative development because it places greater pressure on young adults._|\n|Positive / Negative|_Overall, I view the shift towards cashless payments as positive, provided that alternative options remain available._|\n\n**Không nên:** mở quá xa đề (_Since the beginning of time…_), thay synonyms làm sai nghĩa (_children_ → _juveniles_), hoặc tuyên bố mạnh mà body không bảo vệ được.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E08\n\nVới mỗi prompt, viết **paraphrase (1 câu) → thesis (1 câu) → full introduction (2 câu)**.\n\n1.          _Some people believe that all university courses should be free. Do you agree or disagree?_\n\n2.          _More people use bicycles to travel to work. What are the advantages and disadvantages?_\n\n3.          _Some believe companies should allow flexible hours, while others believe fixed schedules are better. Discuss both views and give your opinion._\n\n4.          _An increasing number of people shop online. Do the benefits outweigh the drawbacks?_\n\n5.          _Young people are spending less time outdoors. What are the causes, and what can be done about this?_\n\n# 9. THESIS STATEMENTS AND A CLEAR POSITION\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nThesis tốt là **câu trả lời**, không chỉ gọi tên chủ đề. Lập trường có thể có điều kiện, nhưng không được thay đổi tùy đoạn.\n\n**Vague:** _This issue has advantages and disadvantages._  \n**Clear:** _Although online learning limits some face-to-face interaction, its greater flexibility and accessibility make it beneficial overall._\n\n**Position ladder:** _I strongly agree…_ (rất đồng tình) → _I largely agree…_ (đồng tình phần lớn) → _I agree to some extent…_ (chỉ đồng tình trong giới hạn đã nêu) → _Although X…, I believe Y…_ (nhượng bộ có định hướng).  \n**Nuance:** _X should complement rather than replace Y_ chỉ hữu ích nếu câu hỏi thực sự là thay thế hoặc kết hợp.\n\n**Consistency test:** Sau mỗi body, hỏi “Đoạn này đang chứng minh phần nào trong thesis?” Nếu không chỉ ra được, body có thể lạc hướng.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E09\n\nSửa các thesis sau thành câu trả lời rõ, có lập trường/điều kiện nếu đề yêu cầu.\n\n1.          _This essay will discuss whether students should wear uniforms._ [Do you agree or disagree?]\n\n2.          _There are good and bad sides of online shopping._ [Do advantages outweigh disadvantages?]\n\n3.          _Both views have their own reasons._ [Discuss both views and give your opinion]\n\n4.          _Traffic is a big issue in cities._ [What causes congestion and how can it be reduced?]\n\n5.          _AI in education is a topic people talk about._ [Is this a positive or negative development?]\n\n# 10. CONCLUSIONS THAT CLOSE THE ARGUMENT\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nConclusion làm hai việc: **restates your answer** + **summarises the most important reason(s)**. Không mở ví dụ hay luận điểm mới; không chép lại introduction nguyên văn.\n\n**Useful, but optional, openings:** _In conclusion,…_; _Overall,…_; _On balance,…_; _For these reasons,…_\n\n**Introduction:** _Although remote work can make teamwork harder, its flexibility and time savings make it beneficial overall._  \n**Matching conclusion:** _Overall, remote work offers clear advantages for employees, particularly by reducing commuting time and allowing greater control over daily schedules. These benefits can outweigh its collaborative challenges when teams communicate effectively._\n\n## Applying Exercise — E10\n\nViết conclusion 1–2 câu **không thêm ý mới** cho các introductions dưới đây.\n\n1.          _I largely support teaching financial literacy at school because it helps students manage everyday decisions and avoid costly mistakes._\n\n2.          _Although online shopping puts pressure on local retailers, I believe its wider choice and convenience bring greater overall benefits._\n\n3.          _Traffic congestion is largely caused by car-dependent urban planning, and the most effective response is to provide reliable alternatives to driving._\n\n# 11. COHERENCE AND COHESION — LOGIC BEFORE CONNECTORS\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n**Coherence** là ý phát triển theo trình tự hiểu được. **Cohesion** là cách ngôn ngữ cho người đọc thấy quan hệ đó. Mạch tốt đến từ **quan hệ ý** trước, linking words sau.\n\n|**Quan hệ**|**Công cụ tự nhiên**|**Khi nào dùng**|\n|---|---|---|\n|Claim → Explanation|_because, since, this is largely because_|Cần trả lời WHY|\n|Cause → Effect|_as a result, which can lead to_|Đã có cơ chế nhân quả|\n|General → Specific|_in particular, for example_|Thu hẹp vào tình huống cụ thể|\n|Concession → Response|_although, admittedly…however_|Thừa nhận rồi đánh giá giới hạn|\n|Compare → Contrast|_while, whereas, compared with_|So sánh theo cùng tiêu chí|\n|Problem → Solution|_to address this, one measure would be_|Biện pháp nhắm đúng nguyên nhân/hậu quả|\n\n**Mechanical paragraph:** _Firstly, public transport is good. Secondly, it is cheap. Furthermore, it is convenient. Moreover, it helps people. Therefore, it is important._\n\n**Natural paragraph:** _Reliable public transport can make daily travel more affordable, especially for residents who do not own a car. When buses and trains run frequently, commuters can reach workplaces and essential services without paying for fuel or parking. This can reduce household transport costs while improving access to opportunities._\n\n**Why better:** Mỗi câu nối bằng nội dung _transport → frequency → no car costs → household impact_, không cần “Firstly, Secondly, Moreover”. Đại từ _This_ có tiền đề rõ: khả năng đi lại mà không phải tự lái và trả chi phí xe.\n\n## Applying Exercise — E11\n\n1.          Xóa connector thừa và ghép thành đoạn tự nhiên: _Firstly, online lessons are flexible. Secondly, students can watch recordings. Moreover, they can review difficult topics. Furthermore, this helps them understand lessons. Therefore, online learning is good._\n\n2.          Sửa đại từ mơ hồ: _Schools should provide tablets to teachers and students because they need them. This will improve it._ Nêu rõ ai cần gì và kết quả nào.\n\n3.          Sắp xếp đúng logic (ghi thứ tự A–D): A _This can reduce the cost of commuting._ / B _Reliable buses may make private cars less necessary._ / C _Workers can then spend less on fuel and parking._ / D _This matters especially to households with limited incomes._\n\n# 12. BAND 7+ GRAMMAR TOOLKIT — GRAMMAR AS MEANING\n\nMỗi cấu trúc bên dưới: **Insight → Framework → Model → Common Mistake → Applying Exercise**. Chỉ sử dụng khi nội dung thực sự cần quan hệ logic đó.\n\n## 12.1 Relative clauses\n\n**Insight:** Nêu chính xác **nhóm người/vật nào**, tránh mọi khẳng định áp dụng cho “everyone”. **Framework:** _People who… may…_; _Policies that… can…_  \n**Model:** _Students who rely too heavily on AI may struggle to develop independent writing skills._  \n**Mistake:** _Students which use AI…_ → _Students who use AI…_  \n**E12.1:** Ghép _Some workers commute long distances. These workers may benefit from remote work._\n\n## 12.2 If-conditionals\n\n**Insight:** Chỉ ra điều kiện thực/giả định. **Framework:** _If + present, … may/will + base verb_; _If + past, … might/would + base verb._  \n**Model:** _If public transport becomes more reliable, some commuters may leave their cars at home._  \n**Mistake:** _If cities will invest…_ (đối với điều kiện loại 1 thông thường).  \n**E12.2:** Hoàn thành _If schools teach students how to verify information, …_\n\n## 12.3 Although / While clauses\n\n**Insight:** Gom hai điểm có quan hệ đối lập vào một câu rõ. **Framework:** _Although X, Y_; _While X, Y._  \n**Model:** _Although online courses are flexible, they offer fewer opportunities for spontaneous interaction._  \n**Mistake:** _Although X, but Y._  \n**E12.3:** Viết câu nhượng bộ về _remote work (flexibility / isolation)_.\n\n## 12.4 By + V-ing\n\n**Insight:** Diễn tả **phương thức**, không chỉ hệ quả. **Framework:** _By + gerund, subject + can/may + verb._  \n**Model:** _By improving bus frequency, cities can make car-free travel more practical._  \n**Mistake:** _By improve bus services, cities…_  \n**E12.4:** Dùng _By + V-ing_ giải thích cách schools improve digital literacy.\n\n## 12.5 Rather than\n\n**Insight:** Phân biệt **thay vì A, ưu tiên B**. **Framework:** _Rather than + V-ing, subject should + verb._  \n**Model:** _Rather than banning technology entirely, schools should teach students how to use it responsibly._  \n**Mistake:** _Rather than to ban technology…_  \n**E12.5:** Viết một giải pháp dùng _Rather than_ cho congestion.\n\n## 12.6 Not only … but also …\n\n**Insight:** Nhấn mạnh hai tác động song song, **không** dùng để làm câu sang trọng. **Framework:** _X not only + verb … but also + verb …_; nếu đặt _Not only_ ở đầu câu cần đảo ngữ.  \n**Model:** _Public libraries not only provide books but also offer quiet places to study._  \n**Mistake:** _Not only libraries provide books…_  \n**E12.6:** Viết câu có chủ ngữ _Volunteering_ và hai lợi ích.\n\n## 12.7 The more …, the more …\n\n**Insight:** Mô tả quan hệ **mức độ tăng cùng nhau**; tránh ngụ ý chắc chắn nếu không có cơ sở. **Framework:** _The more + clause, the more likely + subject + be + to…_  \n**Model:** _The more time students spend practising an argument, the more confident they may become in developing it._  \n**Mistake:** _The more students practice, the more they are confidence._  \n**E12.7:** Viết câu về mức độ reliable buses và willingness to use public transport.\n\n## 12.8 This means that…\n\n**Insight:** Dịch một hệ quả trừu tượng thành **hàm ý cụ thể**. **Framework:** _Sentence. This means that + consequence._  \n**Model:** _Recorded lessons can be replayed at any time. This means that students can revisit difficult explanations at their own pace._  \n**Mistake:** dùng _This_ không rõ đang nhắc điều gì.  \n**E12.8:** Thêm _This means that_ sau _Some employers allow employees to choose their starting hours._\n\n## 12.9 Participle clauses\n\n**Insight:** Rút gọn mệnh đề khi **hai hành động cùng chủ thể** và quan hệ rõ. **Framework:** _By V-ing…_ hoặc _V-ing…, subject…_ (không nhầm mọi participle clause đều là _by_).  \n**Model:** _Living far from major employment centres, many workers spend hours commuting._  \n**Mistake:** _Living far from work, commuting is difficult._ (dangling modifier: “commuting” không phải người sống xa).  \n**E12.9:** Sửa _Using public transport, travel costs can be reduced by workers._\n\n## 12.10 Comparison structures\n\n**Insight:** Đảm bảo hai đối tượng và **tiêu chí so sánh tương ứng**. **Framework:** _X is more + adjective + than Y_; _X offers greater + noun + than Y._  \n**Model:** _For students in remote areas, online courses may offer greater flexibility than traditional classes._  \n**Mistake:** _more easier_, _higher than online learning_ (so sánh sai loại).  \n**E12.10:** So sánh _cycling / driving_ về environmental impact.\n\n## 12.11 Modal verbs\n\n**Insight:** _can_ = khả năng chung; _may/might_ = có thể; _should_ = khuyến nghị; _must_ = nghĩa vụ/điều kiện mạnh. **Framework:** _X may…; Governments should…_  \n**Model:** _Employers should provide guidance because remote staff may feel isolated._  \n**Mistake:** _All students must benefit from online learning._ (khẳng định thiếu cơ sở).  \n**E12.11:** Viết 1 câu dự báo thận trọng và 1 câu khuyến nghị về AI use.\n\n## 12.12 Hedging structures\n\n**Insight:** Dùng mức độ cẩn trọng đúng với bằng chứng; không biến câu nào thành mơ hồ. **Framework:** _tend to_; _may contribute to_; _in some contexts_; _is more likely to_; _can partly explain_.  \n**Model:** _Long working hours may contribute to fatigue, particularly when employees have little control over their schedules._  \n**Mistake:** _Technology always destroys social relationships._  \n**E12.12:** Viết lại _Social media makes teenagers anxious_ theo hướng chính xác hơn.\n\n# 13. HEDGING AND ACADEMIC CAUTION\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nĐánh giá học thuật là **đúng mức độ chắc chắn**. Tránh _everyone, always, never, definitely_ nếu bạn không thể chứng minh. **Không phải** từ nào cũng thay bằng _may_: các sự thật định nghĩa hoặc quan hệ chắc chắn vẫn nên viết rõ.\n\n|**Quá tuyệt đối**|**Chính xác hơn**|**Vì sao**|\n|---|---|---|\n|_Social media causes depression._|_Excessive social media use may contribute to poor mental well-being among some users._|Không khẳng định một nguyên nhân duy nhất|\n|_All children learn better online._|_Some children may benefit from the flexibility of online learning._|Có khác biệt về hoàn cảnh|\n|_Public transport will solve congestion._|_Reliable public transport can help reduce car dependence._|Chính sách không tự động xử lý mọi nguyên nhân|\n|_No one reads books now._|_Reading for pleasure may be less common among some groups._|Tránh khái quát không có dữ liệu|\n\n**Strength ladder:** _will_ (mạnh) → _is likely to_ (khá chắc trong hoàn cảnh phù hợp) → _can_ (khả năng) → _may/might_ (có thể) → _may partly contribute to_ (một phần tác động).\n\n## Applying Exercise — E13\n\nViết lại 10 câu dưới đây, chọn hedging **phù hợp chứ không máy móc**.\n\n1.          _Every student learns better from videos._\n\n2.          _Cars are the only cause of air pollution._\n\n3.          _Online shopping always destroys local businesses._\n\n4.          _Homework never benefits children._\n\n5.          _All employers prefer remote workers._\n\n6.          _AI tools will replace all teachers._\n\n7.          _Teenagers are addicted to their phones._\n\n8.          _The government can eliminate poverty immediately._\n\n9.          _Everyone who lives in a city feels stressed._\n\n10.       _Banning advertisements will solve unhealthy eating._\n\n# 14. NATURAL LANGUAGE BANK — “GEMSTONES” BY FUNCTION\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\n“Gemstone” ở đây chỉ **cụm diễn đạt có thể tái sử dụng**, không phải từ đắt giá để khoe. Mỗi mục bên dưới có **English expression | Nghĩa tiếng Việt | Chức năng | Ví dụ tự nhiên | 1–2 cách diễn đạt khác**. Chọn tối đa 2–3 biểu thức mới mỗi bài và đặt chúng vào đúng quan hệ logic.\n\n|**Expression**|**Nghĩa tiếng Việt**|**Function**|**Natural example**|**Alternatives**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|One compelling reason is that…|Một lý do thuyết phục là…|Claim|_One compelling reason is that buses serve people who cannot drive._|_A key reason is that…; One important factor is…_|\n|A key consideration is that…|Điều cần cân nhắc là…|Claim|_A key consideration is that many students lack reliable internet._|_One issue to consider is…; It is worth noting that…_|\n|One major factor contributing to X is…|Một yếu tố chính góp phần gây X là…|Cause|_One major factor contributing to congestion is poor urban planning._|_A key cause of X is…; X partly results from…_|\n|One significant benefit of X is…|Một lợi ích quan trọng của X là…|Claim|_One significant benefit of remote work is greater flexibility._|_A major advantage is…; X can improve…_|\n|There is a strong case for…|Có lý do thuyết phục để ủng hộ…|Position|_There is a strong case for investing in public libraries._|_It is reasonable to support…; X deserves serious consideration._|\n|This is largely because…|Phần lớn là vì…|Explanation|_This is largely because students need time to revisit difficult lessons._|_The main reason is…; One explanation is…_|\n|One explanation is that…|Một lời giải thích là…|Explanation|_One explanation is that housing near offices has become expensive._|_This may be because…; A possible reason is…_|\n|This may partly stem from…|Điều này phần nào bắt nguồn từ…|Cause|_The trend may partly stem from rising living costs._|_This may be linked to…; One contributing factor is…_|\n|This often occurs when…|Điều này thường xảy ra khi…|Mechanism|_This often occurs when workers cannot find affordable homes nearby._|_In situations where…; When…_|\n|In practical terms,…|Trên thực tế / xét về thực hiện…|Mechanism|_In practical terms, students could review recorded lessons after class._|_In everyday situations,…; More specifically,…_|\n|By doing so,…|Bằng cách đó…|Mechanism|_Schools can teach source-checking. By doing so, they can reduce blind reliance on AI._|_This would allow…; As a result of this measure,…_|\n|When X happens, Y is more likely to…|Khi X xảy ra, Y có khả năng…|Mechanism|_When buses are reliable, commuters are more likely to use them._|_If X occurs, Y may…; X can make Y more likely._|\n|As a result,…|Kết quả là…|Consequence|_As a result, families may spend less on transport._|_Consequently,…; This can lead to…_|\n|This can in turn lead to…|Việc này tiếp tục dẫn đến…|Consequence|_Less sleep can in turn lead to poorer concentration._|_This may then cause…; Over time, this can…_|\n|Over the longer term,…|Về dài hạn…|Long-term effect|_Over the longer term, regular reading may strengthen language skills._|_In the long run,…; Over time,…_|\n|The cumulative impact can be significant.|Tác động tích lũy có thể đáng kể.|Evaluation|_Small delays occur daily, and the cumulative impact can be significant._|_These effects may add up.; The combined effect may be substantial._|\n|For example,…|Ví dụ…|Example|_For example, a rural student could join an online science class._|_For instance,…; Consider a student who…_|\n|This can be illustrated by…|Có thể minh họa bằng…|Example|_This can be illustrated by a worker who saves an hour each day._|_One example is…; Consider, for example,…_|\n|Admittedly,…|Phải thừa nhận rằng…|Concession|_Admittedly, online classes can limit social interaction._|_It is true that…; Although…_|\n|There is some merit in the argument that…|Quan điểm rằng… có phần hợp lý|Concession|_There is some merit in the argument that exams encourage discipline._|_This concern is valid to some extent.; Although X may be true,…_|\n|Although it is true that…|Dù đúng là…|Concession|_Although it is true that phones can distract students, they can support research._|_While X is true,…; Admittedly,…_|\n|However, this overlooks the fact that…|Tuy nhiên, điều này bỏ qua thực tế là…|Counterargument|_However, this overlooks the fact that some learners have no access to tutors._|_This fails to consider…; A limitation is that…_|\n|This argument is limited because…|Lập luận này có giới hạn vì…|Counterargument|_This argument is limited because it assumes everyone owns a car._|_One weakness is…; This view does not account for…_|\n|Focusing solely on X would be too narrow an approach.|Chỉ tập trung vào X là cách tiếp cận quá hẹp.|Counterargument|_Focusing solely on punishment would be too narrow an approach._|_X alone may be insufficient.; A broader response is needed._|\n|This is particularly important because…|Điều này đặc biệt quan trọng vì…|Evaluation|_This is particularly important because rural students have fewer alternatives._|_This matters because…; The significance lies in…_|\n|This is especially concerning because…|Điều này đặc biệt đáng lo vì…|Evaluation|_This is especially concerning because children are still developing self-control._|_This raises concerns because…; The risk is greater when…_|\n|The broader significance is that…|Ý nghĩa rộng hơn là…|Evaluation|_The broader significance is that access need not depend on location._|_More importantly,…; This matters beyond…_|\n|For this reason,…|Vì lý do này…|Inference|_For this reason, schools should provide clear guidelines._|_Therefore,…; This suggests that…_|\n|One practical measure would be to…|Một biện pháp khả thi là…|Solution|_One practical measure would be to increase bus frequency._|_A useful first step is…; Governments could…_|\n|A more effective approach would be to…|Cách tiếp cận hiệu quả hơn là…|Solution|_A more effective approach would be to combine training with clear rules._|_It would be better to…; A stronger response is…_|\n|Rather than relying solely on X,…|Thay vì chỉ dựa vào X…|Balanced solution|_Rather than relying solely on fines, cities could improve bus services._|_In addition to X,…; X alone is not enough._|\n|X should complement rather than replace Y.|X nên bổ trợ thay vì thay thế Y.|Balanced solution|_AI feedback should complement rather than replace teacher guidance._|_X should be used alongside Y.; Y remains essential even when X is used._|\n|On balance,…|Cân nhắc tổng thể…|Judgement|_On balance, the benefits of flexible work are greater for many employees._|_Overall,…; Taking both sides into account,…_|\n|Provided that…|Với điều kiện rằng…|Qualified position|_Online assessment can work well provided that identity checks are reliable._|_As long as…; If…_|\n\n## Applying Exercise — E14\n\nChọn biểu thức phù hợp (không cần dùng đúng một đáp án):\n\n1.          Viết một câu thừa nhận điểm mạnh của đối phương rồi giới hạn nó (_Concession + response_).\n\n2.          Diễn tả _housing costs → move farther away → longer commute_ bằng **mechanism**, không dùng _Moreover_.\n\n3.          Thêm evaluation vào _Libraries provide free internet access._\n\n4.          Viết một câu giải pháp _training should not fully replace teacher feedback_.\n\n5.          Viết một kết luận _outweigh_ có tiêu chí **who benefits** hoặc **how long effects last**.\n\n# 15. DIAGNOSTIC — 20 COMMON VIETNAMESE LEARNER ERRORS\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nBốn cột giúp tự sửa: **WRONG / WHY IT IS WEAK / BETTER / NATURAL, MORE DEVELOPED VERSION**. Cột cuối là một hướng cải thiện, không phải mẫu phải sao chép.\n\n|**# & Error**|**WRONG**|**WHY IT IS WEAK**|**BETTER**|**NATURAL, MORE DEVELOPED VERSION**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1. Dịch từng chữ|_People are more and more pressure._|Thiếu collocation và loại từ|_People face increasing pressure._|_Many employees face growing pressure to meet demanding targets._|\n|2. Câu dài mất kiểm soát|_Students use AI it is fast but they do not check so information wrong._|Run-on; chủ ngữ và quan hệ mơ hồ|_AI is fast, but students may not check its output._|_Although AI can generate answers quickly, students may rely on inaccurate information if they fail to verify it._|\n|3. Mở bài học thuộc|_Nowadays, in this modern society, X is a hot topic._|Chung chung, không trả lời task|_The use of AI in schools is widely debated._|_While some favour banning AI in schools, I believe supervised use is a more effective response._|\n|4. Topic sentence yếu|_Transport has a lot of problems._|Không có claim cụ thể|_Traffic congestion wastes commuters’ time._|_Heavy congestion can undermine productivity by making daily journeys less predictable._|\n|5. Lặp lại ý|_Exams are stressful because they cause stress._|Explanation không thêm điều mới|_High-stakes exams create pressure._|_When admission depends on a single test, students may fear that one poor result will limit their options._|\n|6. Ví dụ trước giải thích|_Public transport is useful. For example, Bus 10._|Ví dụ không có WHY/HOW|_Public transport offers affordable travel._|_Frequent buses make commuting cheaper for people without cars, as illustrated by workers who can avoid fuel and parking costs._|\n|7. Lấy ví dụ thay luận điểm|_AI helps learners. For example, ChatGPT._|Tên sản phẩm không chứng minh cơ chế|_AI can provide immediate practice feedback._|_An AI tutor can explain mistakes during practice, allowing students to correct misunderstandings before the next lesson._|\n|8. Quá nhiều connectors|_Firstly,… Secondly,… Moreover,… Furthermore,…_|Nối hình thức, ý không phát triển|Dùng quan hệ cause–effect thật|_Reliable buses reduce dependence on cars, which can lower commuting costs for some households._|\n|9. Khẳng định tuyệt đối|_All teenagers are addicted to phones._|Thiếu căn cứ và phạm vi|_Some teenagers use phones excessively._|_Excessive smartphone use may disrupt sleep for some teenagers._|\n|10. Từ quá thân mật|_Kids get super stressed out by exams._|Register chưa phù hợp|_Children may experience exam stress._|_High-stakes examinations can place considerable pressure on students._|\n|11. Collocation sai|_do a decision; make pollution_|Kết hợp từ không tự nhiên|_make a decision; cause pollution_|_Poor transport planning can contribute to air pollution and limit travel choices._|\n|12. Đại từ mơ hồ|_They need it, and this helps them._|_They/it/this_ không rõ|Gọi tên đối tượng|_Students need clear feedback, which can help them improve their writing._|\n|13. Nhầm noun/verb|_The develop of cities…_|Sai loại từ|_The development of cities…_|_Rapid urban development can increase pressure on housing and transport._|\n|14. Subject–verb|_Online classes provides flexibility._|Chủ ngữ số nhiều|_Online classes provide flexibility._|_Online classes provide flexibility for students with irregular schedules._|\n|15. Articles|_Government should improve public transport._|Thiếu article khi nói đến chính phủ cụ thể|_The government should improve public transport._|_Governments should invest in services that make commuting more reliable._|\n|16. Countable/uncountable|_Many informations are useful._|_Information_ không đếm được|_Much information is useful._|_Students need reliable information rather than simply a large quantity of content._|\n|17. Nhồi từ khó|_The quintessential amelioration of scholastic paradigms…_|Khó hiểu, không chính xác mục đích|_Improving education…_|_Improving access to qualified teachers can help reduce educational inequality._|\n|18. Quá nhiều ý|_Work from home saves time, cuts costs, reduces traffic, improves health, helps family and boosts GDP._|Sáu claim không có HOW|Chọn một claim|_Remote work can improve work-life balance by reducing the time employees spend commuting._|\n|19. Mất stance|_I strongly agree… / However, I totally disagree…_|Không giữ lập trường|_I largely agree, although…_|_I support flexible work overall, despite some concerns about collaboration._|\n|20. Trả lời topic, không trả lời task|Đề hỏi _outweigh_, bài chỉ liệt kê pros/cons|Thiếu so sánh bên nào mạnh hơn|Phải kết luận _which side outweighs_|_Although online shopping can hurt local retailers, its wider accessibility and choice make the benefits greater overall._|\n\n## Applying Exercise — E15\n\n**Diagnose and repair.** Với mỗi câu sau, ghi **mã lỗi** từ 1–20, sửa câu, rồi thêm **một bước WHY/HOW** nếu còn thiếu:\n\nA. _Nowadays, technology is very good and important in our modern world._  \nB. _Students can using AI to find many informations._  \nC. _Public transport is good because it has many benefits._  \nD. _The government must ban all cars to completely solve pollution._  \nE. _Many jobs are stressful. Moreover, people are stressed. Furthermore, stress is common._\n\n# 16. QUESTION-TYPE MASTER PRACTICE — 12 GUIDED MINI TASKS\n\n## Knowledge / Insight\n\nTất cả dạng đề đều tuân theo cùng nguyên tắc **hiểu câu hỏi trước khi viết**. Nhưng bước “Opinion” có thể là **not required** nếu đề chỉ yêu cầu giải thích hiện tượng/quan điểm. Với 12 đề dưới đây, học viên không viết 12 bài toàn phần; mục tiêu là **12 bản kế hoạch + 1 body paragraph cho mỗi loại**.\n\n**Phiếu hướng dẫn áp dụng cho TỪNG đề E16.1–E16.12:**\n\n1.          **Identify Task:** Gạch keyword; ghi task 1/task 2 nếu có: __________________.\n\n2.          **Choose Position:** Required / optional? Nếu cần, câu trả lời của bạn: __________________.\n\n3.          **Brainstorm:** 3–4 hướng ban đầu: __________________.\n\n4.          **Select Best Ideas:** Giữ 2 ý dễ bảo vệ nhất, gạch bỏ ý chung chung: __________________.\n\n5.          **Develop Argument 1:** WHAT → WHY → HOW → RESULT → (EXAMPLE/EVALUATION): __________________.\n\n6.          **Develop Argument 2:** WHAT → WHY → HOW → RESULT → (EXAMPLE/EVALUATION): __________________.\n\n7.          **Write Thesis:** Một câu trả lời đúng yêu cầu: __________________.\n\n8.          **Write Topic Sentences:** B1: __________________. B2: __________________.\n\n9.          **Build Body Paragraph:** Chọn một argument, viết đoạn 85–115 từ: __________________.\n\n10.       **Self-check:** Có trả lời đủ task? Có lập trường nếu cần? Có ít nhất một HOW? Ví dụ có liên quan? Câu văn tự nhiên và kiểm soát được?\n\n**Lưu ý:** Các gợi ý trong mỗi mini task chỉ giúp khởi động tư duy, **không phải đáp án**. Đáp án tham khảo của cả 12 nằm ở mục 18.\n\n### E16.1 — Agree / Disagree\n\n_Schools should require all students to learn basic money-management skills. Do you agree or disagree?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Những quyết định tài chính nào học sinh thật sự phải đưa ra? Ai hưởng lợi? Có vấn đề gì nếu bắt buộc nhưng dạy thiếu thực hành?  \n**Student plan:** Opinion: ______ | 4 brainstormed ideas: ______ | Best 2: ______ | Why/How 1: ______ | Why/How 2: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2 claims: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.2 — To What Extent\n\n_The main responsibility for protecting the environment lies with individuals rather than governments. To what extent do you agree or disagree?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Phân biệt điều cá nhân thay đổi được và điều cần quy định/hạ tầng. Nếu _partly agree_, giới hạn ở đâu?  \n**Student plan:** Extent: ______ | Individual mechanism: ______ | Government mechanism: ______ | Best 2: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.3 — Discuss Both Views\n\n_Some people believe students learn more effectively through group projects, while others favour individual assignments. Discuss both views._\n\n**Guided prompts:** Mỗi cách phát triển kỹ năng nào? Vì sao? Đừng mặc định cần nêu personal opinion.  \n**Student plan:** View A: ______ | View B: ______ | WHY/HOW for A: ______ | WHY/HOW for B: ______ | Neutral thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.4 — Discuss Both Views and Give Your Opinion\n\n_Some people believe children should start learning a foreign language in primary school, while others think they should begin in secondary school. Discuss both views and give your opinion._\n\n**Guided prompts:** Sớm: exposure/practice? Muộn: readiness/qualified teachers? Bạn chọn bên nào và vì sao?  \n**Student plan:** View A: ______ | View B: ______ | Your view: ______ | WHY/HOW x2: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.5 — Advantages and Disadvantages\n\n_What are the advantages and disadvantages of taking university courses online?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Một advantage có điều kiện, một disadvantage cụ thể. Không cần khẳng định bên nào “outweighs”.  \n**Student plan:** Advantage: ______ | Disadvantage: ______ | Mechanism 1: ______ | Mechanism 2: ______ | Balanced thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.6 — Outweigh\n\n_More companies are adopting a four-day working week. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Ai được lợi? Khi nào productivity giữ ổn định? Hạn chế trong dịch vụ cần trực liên tục? Dùng tiêu chí đánh giá rõ.  \n**Student plan:** Pro: ______ | Con: ______ | Weighing criterion: ______ | Overall judgement: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.7 — Problems and Solutions\n\n_Many large cities have too few affordable homes. What problems does this cause, and how can they be addressed?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Problem là hệ quả gì của thiếu nhà giá phù hợp? Solution phải tác động được vào hệ quả/nguồn cung.  \n**Student plan:** Problem: ______ | How harm develops: ______ | Practical measure: ______ | How measure works: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.8 — Causes and Solutions\n\n_Young adults in many countries are exercising less than before. What are the main causes, and how can this be addressed?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Nguyên nhân về lịch làm việc, môi trường di chuyển, khả năng tiếp cận; tránh nói “lazy people”.  \n**Student plan:** Cause: ______ | Mechanism: ______ | Targeted solution: ______ | Expected result: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.9 — Causes and Effects\n\n_In some countries, people are having fewer children. What are the causes and effects of this trend?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Chi phí, thời gian, ưu tiên cá nhân; hậu quả ở hộ gia đình, lực lượng lao động. **Không cần viết giải pháp.**  \n**Student plan:** Cause: ______ | How it changes decisions: ______ | Effect: ______ | How effect emerges: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.10 — Two-Part Questions\n\n_Many people rely on online reviews before buying products. Why is this common? Should consumers trust these reviews?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Q1 hỏi động cơ; Q2 hỏi mức độ tin cậy và điều kiện. Tránh chỉ bàn pros/cons của online shopping.  \n**Student plan:** Answer Q1: ______ | Answer Q2: ______ | WHY/HOW x2: ______ | Thesis (both answers): ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.11 — Positive or Negative Development\n\n_More people are using digital payment methods instead of cash. Is this a positive or negative development?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Đánh giá theo tiện lợi, tiếp cận, nguy cơ bị loại trừ. Có thể chọn _positive with safeguards_.  \n**Student plan:** Evaluation: ______ | Benefit/risk 1: ______ | Benefit/risk 2: ______ | Condition (if any): ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n### E16.12 — Mixed / Hybrid\n\n_Why are more people choosing private cars over public transport, and should governments introduce measures to discourage car use?_\n\n**Guided prompts:** Yêu cầu 1 = cause; yêu cầu 2 = policy opinion. Biện pháp phải giải quyết _WHY people choose cars_.  \n**Student plan:** Cause: ______ | Mechanism: ______ | Policy judgement: ______ | Measure/how: ______ | Thesis: ______ | B1/B2: ______ | Paragraph: ______.\n\n# 17. FULL TASK 2 APPLICATION — COMPLETE ONE ESSAY\n\n## Exam-style question\n\n**Some people believe that schools should teach students how to use artificial intelligence (AI) tools, while others think these tools should be banned in classrooms. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.**\n\n**Target:** 260–290 words, about 40 minutes. **Do not read Section 18 before completing your draft.**\n\n## Stage 1 — Analyse the Question (3 minutes)\n\n•           **Topic:** _______________________________\n\n•           **Task:** _______________________________\n\n•           **Scope:** _______________________________\n\n•           **Position (your answer):** _______________________________\n\n•           **Keywords to underline:** _______________________________\n\n## Stage 2 — Brainstorm (2 minutes)\n\nGhi **4–6 ý thô**, chưa viết câu dài. Ví dụ nhóm khía cạnh có thể cân nhắc: learning support, academic integrity, over-reliance, digital literacy, teacher supervision, equal access. Không cần dùng hết.\n\n1.          __________ 2. __________ 3. __________ 4. __________ 5. __________ 6. __________\n\n## Stage 3 — Select (1 minute)\n\nGiữ **hai ý phát triển được** để mỗi đoạn có một trọng tâm. Gạch ý trùng hoặc không liên quan trực tiếp đến câu hỏi _teach vs ban_.  \n**Keep for View 1:** ______. **Keep for View 2 + opinion:** ______.  \n**Remove because too vague/repetitive:** ______.\n\n## Stage 4 — Build Arguments (4 minutes)\n\n|**Thinking step**|**Body 1 — BAN**|**Body 2 — TEACH WITH GUIDANCE**|\n|---|---|---|\n|WHAT|______|______|\n|WHY|______|______|\n|HOW|______|______|\n|RESULT|______|______|\n|EXAMPLE (optional)|______|______|\n|WHY IT MATTERS|______|______|\n\n**Important:** Body 1 phải trình bày _best version_ của bên ủng hộ ban, không biến họ thành người thiếu hiểu biết. Body 2 phải nói rõ tại sao bạn **đồng tình/không đồng tình**, không chỉ kể lại view còn lại.\n\n## Stage 5 — Build Thesis (1 minute)\n\n**Thesis answering both views and your own opinion:**  \n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n## Stage 6 — Topic Sentences (1 minute)\n\n**Body 1 (why some support banning):** ____________________________________  \n**Body 2 (why supervised teaching is preferable / your chosen view):** ____________________________________\n\n## Stage 7 — Body Paragraph 1 (8 minutes)\n\nViết 90–105 từ. Bắt đầu bằng claim về view ban. Trình bày **why, mechanism, result**, sau đó 1 ví dụ hoặc đánh giá.  \n**Draft:**\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n## Stage 8 — Body Paragraph 2 (8 minutes)\n\nViết 100–115 từ. Trình bày view _teach_, phát triển cơ chế _how guided AI use improves learning/critical checking_, rồi nêu vì sao bạn chọn.  \n**Draft:**\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n## Stage 9 — Introduction (3 minutes)\n\nKhoảng 35–45 từ; paraphrase đúng _banned in classrooms_ chứ không phải _banned everywhere_; nói rõ stance.  \n**Draft:** ……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n## Stage 10 — Conclusion (2 minutes)\n\nKhoảng 30–40 từ; tổng hợp hai sides và chốt, không thêm ý mới.  \n**Draft:** ……………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\n## Stage 11 — Write / Assemble the Complete Essay (4 minutes)\n\nChép hoặc chỉnh lại thành 4 đoạn mạch lạc, mục tiêu **260–290 từ**. Kiểm tra điều kiện tối thiểu **250 từ** của bài thi. Không ép mọi câu phải phức.\n\n## Stage 12 — Self-check (3 minutes)\n\n|**Criterion**|**Yes / Needs work**|**Specific revision**|\n|---|---|---|\n|Task Response: đã giải thích **cả hai views**?|______|______|\n|Task Response: own opinion rõ ở I, B2, C?|______|______|\n|Task Response: ít nhất một WHY + HOW thật sự?|______|______|\n|Coherence: B1 và B2 có trọng tâm riêng?|______|______|\n|Coherence: ví dụ theo sau và minh họa đúng argument?|______|______|\n|Lexical Resource: _ban, allow, supervise, verify, reliance_ dùng đúng nghĩa?|______|______|\n|Lexical Resource: không lặp _good/bad/important_ vô ích?|______|______|\n|Grammar: dấu câu; S–V agreement; articles; conditionals?|______|______|\n|Grammar: đại từ _this/they_ có tham chiếu rõ?|______|______|\n|Full response: ≥250 words; 4 đoạn; không thêm claim ở conclusion?|______|______|\n\n**Teacher marking grid (formative, not an official IELTS score):** TR ____ / CC ____ / LR ____ / GRA ____; **One strength:** ______; **One priority to revise:** ______.\n\n# 18. TEACHER’S ANSWER KEY — SUGGESTED ANSWERS\n\n**Tất cả đáp án dưới đây đều là gợi ý; những cách diễn đạt khác vẫn đúng nếu liên quan đề, có logic và diễn đạt chính xác. Không chấm học viên theo việc giống hệt câu mẫu.**\n\n## Key E01 — From idea to argument\n\n**1. Public transport** — Claim: _Reliable public transport makes commuting more affordable._ WHY: _Owning a car can be expensive._ HOW: _Passengers avoid fuel, parking and maintenance costs._ RESULT: _They can spend less on daily travel._ EXAMPLE: _A worker may take a monthly bus pass instead of driving._ EVALUATION: _This matters most to lower-income households._\n\n**2. Working from home** — Claim: _Remote work can improve work-life balance._ WHY: _Commuting takes time._ HOW: _Workers can use that time for rest or family._ RESULT: _Daily schedules become more manageable._ EXAMPLE: _A parent may collect a child from school without a long return journey._ EVALUATION: _Greater flexibility can ease pressure on working families._\n\n**3. Exams** — Claim: _High-stakes exams can create considerable pressure._ WHY: _A single result may affect admission opportunities._ HOW: _Students may see mistakes as a threat to their future._ RESULT: _Anxiety can make preparation less effective._ EXAMPLE: _A student may struggle to sleep before an entrance test._ EVALUATION: _Assessment design matters when the consequences are substantial._\n\n## Key E02 — 12 types: identification, opinion and sample thesis\n\n|**Type**|**Required response**|**Opinion?**|**Safe paragraph map / one-sentence thesis example**|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|2.1 Agree / Disagree|Support/reject free transport policy|Yes|I: stance; B1 accessibility; B2 cost/funding condition; C stance. _I support cheaper public transport, although making it entirely free may place too much pressure on public budgets._|\n|2.2 Extent|Degree to which employment is education’s main purpose|Yes|I largely disagree; B1 employment skills; B2 citizenship/critical thinking; C. _Although education should prepare students for work, I do not believe employment should be its main purpose._|\n|2.3 Both views|Explain home vs school learning|Not explicitly|I debate; B1 home personal attention; B2 school social support; C synthesis. _Home learning can offer individual attention, whereas schools provide structured teaching and social interaction._|\n|2.4 Both + opinion|Explain ban and learning-tool views, then choose|Yes|I favor supervised use; B1 distraction; B2 purposeful learning; C. _Although smartphone bans can reduce distractions, I favour controlled classroom use because phones can support specific learning activities._|\n|2.5 Adv / Disadv|Benefit and drawback of remote work|Not explicitly|I identify both; B1 flexibility; B2 social isolation; C summary. _Remote work provides schedule flexibility but may reduce everyday collaboration among colleagues._|\n|2.6 Outweigh|Both sides + weigh which matters more|Yes|I benefits outweigh; B1 shop pressure; B2 access/choice + comparison; C. _Although online shopping can harm some local retailers, its accessibility and convenience bring greater benefits to consumers overall._|\n|2.7 Problems / Solutions|Congestion consequences + matched remedies|Not required as stance|I problem/response; B1 wasted time/pollution; B2 reliable mass transit; C. _Congestion wastes time and worsens air quality, and reliable public transport could reduce both effects._|\n|2.8 Causes / Solutions|Why science enrolment drops + specific remedy|Not required as stance|I causes/response; B1 abstract teaching; B2 experiments/career guidance; C. _A lack of practical exposure may discourage students from science, so schools should connect lessons with real applications._|\n|2.9 Causes / Effects|Why reading falls + outcomes|No|I trend; B1 competing digital entertainment; B2 weaker sustained reading; C. _The decline may be partly linked to digital entertainment, with possible consequences for sustained reading habits._|\n|2.10 Two-part|Why people live alone + positive/negative|Yes to Q2|I financial independence and mixed/negative evaluation; B1 causes; B2 judgement; C. _Living alone is increasingly common because of greater independence, but it can be harmful when it leads to prolonged isolation._|\n|2.11 Positive / Negative|Overall appraisal of online courses|Yes|I positive with condition; B1 access; B2 interaction limitations/mitigation; C. _I see online courses as a positive development, provided that learners still receive meaningful feedback and support._|\n|2.12 Hybrid|Problems of fast fashion + who has responsibility|Yes, responsibility judgement|I environmental harms + shared responsibility; B1 waste/pollution; B2 manufacturers/regulators/consumers; C. _Fast fashion creates substantial waste, and both producers and governments should take primary responsibility for reducing it._|\n\n**Quick distinction keys:** 2.3 does **not** explicitly require own opinion; 2.4 does. 2.5 requires both sides but no weighing; 2.6 **must** weigh. 2.1 and 2.2 both require a clear position; 2.2 stresses its degree. Với mỗi ví dụ B, đáp án có thể khác nếu thực hiện đúng task.\n\n## Key E03 — Four-step analysis (possible answers)\n\n|**Q**|**Topic**|**Task**|**Scope**|**Position / answer**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|School curriculum|Extent of agreement|Financial literacy as part of school education|_I strongly agree because students need practical money-management skills._|\n|2|Remote work|Benefits and drawbacks|Company policies allowing home-based work|_Flexibility is a major benefit, while reduced collaboration is a drawback._|\n|3|Urban travel|Causes + positive/negative|Growing cycling use in cities|_Better cycle routes may explain the trend; it is positive overall._|\n|4|Teenagers’ time|Discuss both views + opinion|Volunteering versus academic focus|_Both have value, but limited volunteering alongside study is preferable._|\n|5|Plastic pollution|Causes + solutions|Growth in plastic waste, not pollution in general|_Single-use packaging contributes to waste; reusable systems and producer rules can help._|\n\n## Key E04 — Four argument chains\n\n**1. Libraries:** Claim _Free libraries improve access to learning._ → WHY _Books and internet access can be expensive._ → HOW _Libraries provide shared resources without direct usage fees._ → Immediate _Residents can study and search for information._ → Long-term _Some may gain stronger skills and more options._ → Example _A job seeker can use a library computer to complete applications._ → Matters _Access to opportunities becomes less dependent on income._\n\n**2. Commutes:** Claim _Long commutes may harm well-being._ → WHY _Travel consumes time needed for rest._ → HOW _Workers arrive home late and have limited recovery time._ → Immediate _Fatigue rises._ → Long-term _Work–life balance may worsen._ → Example _A commuter spends two hours on buses each day._ → Matters _The effect is repeated across a working week._\n\n**3. Uniforms:** Claim _Uniforms may reduce visible differences in spending on clothes._ → WHY _Brand-name outfits can signal family income._ → HOW _A shared dress code limits daily clothing comparisons._ → Immediate _Appearance-related pressure may fall._ → Long-term _Students may feel more included._ → Example _Classmates wear the same basic school outfit._ → Matters _School belonging should not depend on buying expensive clothes._\n\n**4. AI reliance:** Claim _Uncritical AI use may weaken independent learning._ → WHY _Ready-made answers remove some need to work through problems._ → HOW _Students copy solutions before testing their understanding._ → Immediate _Less independent practice._ → Long-term _Difficulty explaining ideas without help._ → Example _A student submits an AI-written paragraph but cannot defend its claims._ → Matters _Schools must assess learning, not just polished output._\n\n## Key E05 — Sentence function exercises\n\n|**Ex.**|**One possible answer**|\n|---|---|\n|5.1|_Practical education can help students make more informed financial decisions._ / _A major challenge facing cities is the shortage of affordable housing._|\n|5.2|_Public libraries matter to low-income families because they provide books, study spaces and internet access without charging users directly._|\n|5.3|_Poor public transport can encourage greater car use. This may in turn contribute to congestion during peak hours._|\n|5.4|_High housing costs → workers move farther from offices → longer commutes._ / _Regular reading → repeated exposure to words in context → stronger vocabulary._|\n|5.5|_Residents may use cars for even short trips, increasing traffic volumes. Over time, this can make air quality and street safety worse._|\n|5.6|_For example, a nurse who takes a reliable bus to work may avoid paying for parking every day._|\n|5.7|_Without clear rules on AI use, students may submit answers they do not understand._ / _If employers offered flexible hours, staff could avoid the busiest commuting periods._|\n|5.8|_Online lessons generally offer greater scheduling flexibility than face-to-face classes, although the latter provide more direct interaction._|\n|5.9|_While city residents may have greater access to jobs, people in rural areas often benefit from quieter surroundings._|\n|5.10|_Admittedly, banning phones can reduce distractions. However, supervised use may help students learn to assess digital information critically._|\n|5.11|_Rest is important, but removing all homework overlooks the value of short, purposeful practice tasks._|\n|5.12|_This matters because limited family time can affect relationships and increase the pressure parents experience on working days._|\n|5.13|_City authorities could introduce frequent buses on busy routes so commuters have a practical alternative to driving, potentially reducing congestion._|\n\n## Key E06 — One developed paragraph\n\n_Part-time jobs can help university students become more independent. Many students have limited opportunities to practise workplace communication and time management during their courses. By working a few hours each week, they can learn to deal with customers, cooperate with colleagues and organise their schedules around deadlines. These experiences may increase their confidence when they apply for full-time positions. This is particularly useful for students who have little previous work experience, provided that employment does not interfere with their studies._\n\n**Teacher question:** HOW nằm ở _By working a few hours each week…_. Không cần nêu thêm 3 lợi ích khác trong đoạn này.\n\n## Key E07 — Progressive body paragraph\n\n•           **Claim:** _Remote work can help employees manage family responsibilities more effectively._\n\n•           **WHY:** _Fixed office schedules and long commutes leave little time for everyday tasks._\n\n•           **HOW:** _Working at home can free up travel time and allow more control over daily routines._\n\n•           **RESULT:** _Some workers may feel less pressure when balancing professional and personal demands._\n\n•           **EVALUATION:** _This is especially useful for employees who care for children or older relatives._\n\n**Sample paragraph:** _One meaningful benefit of remote work is that it can make family responsibilities easier to manage. Employees who travel long distances to an office often have little flexibility when arranging school pickups or medical appointments. By working from home, they can avoid some commuting time and plan routine responsibilities around their working hours. This may reduce the strain of balancing family and professional demands, particularly for people who care for children or older relatives. However, this benefit depends on employers setting realistic expectations about availability and working hours._\n\n## Key E08 — Five two-sentence introductions\n\n1.          _Whether universities should charge tuition fees remains widely debated. I support greater public funding, but I do not believe making every course free is always the fairest use of limited resources._\n\n2.          _Cycling to work is becoming a more common choice in some places. It can reduce commuting costs and vehicle emissions, although road safety and weather remain practical concerns._\n\n3.          _Employers differ on whether staff should work flexible or fixed hours. Although fixed schedules make coordination easier, I believe flexible hours are generally preferable when responsibilities are clearly defined._\n\n4.          _Online shopping is changing how people buy everyday products. Despite the pressure it may place on local retailers, its accessibility and broad selection make its benefits greater overall._\n\n5.          _Many young people now spend less time outdoors. This may partly result from screen-based entertainment and limited safe spaces, and a combination of school activities and community facilities could help reverse the trend._\n\n## Key E09 — Clear theses\n\n1.          _I support school uniforms because they may reduce visible clothing-related differences and simplify students’ daily routines._\n\n2.          _Although online shopping creates challenges for physical shops, I believe its convenience and wider choice outweigh these drawbacks for many consumers._\n\n3.          _Both approaches offer benefits, but I favour flexible working arrangements because employees can better manage personal responsibilities._\n\n4.          _Urban congestion is often driven by car-dependent planning, and governments should improve public transport to make alternatives to driving more attractive._\n\n5.          _I consider supervised AI use in education a positive development because it can support learning while helping students develop critical checking skills._\n\n## Key E10 — Matching conclusions\n\n1.          _In conclusion, financial education deserves a place in the school curriculum because it can help students handle everyday expenses and make more informed decisions._\n\n2.          _On balance, online shopping offers greater overall benefits through convenience and product choice, although support may still be needed for local retailers._\n\n3.          _Overall, reducing congestion requires cities to address their dependence on private cars by providing reliable, affordable and practical alternatives._\n\n## Key E11 — Natural cohesion\n\n**1.** _Online lessons can be useful because students are often able to revisit recorded material. When a topic is difficult, they can pause a lesson and review the explanation at their own pace. This flexibility may help them understand ideas that they missed the first time._\n\n**2.** _Schools could provide teachers with tablets for classroom demonstrations and give students access to shared devices for guided practice. These resources could make digital learning activities more accessible, provided that staff receive appropriate training._\n\n**3.** **B → C → A → D** is acceptable: _Reliable buses may make private cars less necessary. Workers can then spend less on fuel and parking. This can reduce the cost of commuting. This matters especially to households with limited incomes._ A/C may swap if the referents are made clear.\n\n## Key E12 — Grammar toolkit\n\n|**Ex.**|**Suggested correction / completion**|\n|---|---|\n|12.1|_Workers who commute long distances may benefit from remote work._|\n|12.2|_If schools teach students how to verify information, they may become less dependent on unreliable online claims._|\n|12.3|_Although remote work offers flexibility, some employees may feel socially isolated._|\n|12.4|_By teaching students how to check online sources, schools can improve digital literacy._|\n|12.5|_Rather than expanding roads alone, cities should invest in frequent and reliable buses._|\n|12.6|_Volunteering not only develops communication skills but also helps students understand community needs._|\n|12.7|_The more reliable bus services become, the more willing some commuters may be to use public transport._|\n|12.8|_This means that employees may be able to avoid rush-hour journeys._|\n|12.9|_By using public transport, workers can reduce their travel costs._|\n|12.10|_Cycling generally creates fewer direct emissions than driving a petrol-powered car._|\n|12.11|_AI may help students practise independently, but schools should set clear rules for responsible use._|\n|12.12|_Heavy social media use may contribute to anxiety among some teenagers, particularly when it encourages unhealthy comparisons._|\n\n## Key E13 — Ten hedging rewrites\n\n1.          _Some students may learn more effectively from videos, especially when lessons contain demonstrations._\n\n2.          _Car use can contribute significantly to air pollution in busy cities._\n\n3.          _Online shopping can put pressure on local retailers, particularly smaller stores._\n\n4.          _Excessive homework may be unhelpful, although short practice activities can support learning._\n\n5.          _Some employers may prefer remote arrangements when tasks can be completed independently._\n\n6.          _AI tools may take over certain routine teaching tasks, but teachers still play an important role._\n\n7.          _Some teenagers may spend more time on their phones than is healthy._\n\n8.          _Government policies can reduce poverty over time, but immediate elimination is unlikely._\n\n9.          _Living in a large city can be stressful for some people because of congestion and high living costs._\n\n10.       _Restricting certain food advertisements may help improve eating habits, but it is unlikely to solve the problem alone._\n\n## Key E14 — Gemstone application\n\n1.          _Admittedly, private cars offer greater flexibility. However, this overlooks the fact that many residents cannot afford to drive._\n\n2.          _When housing near city centres becomes unaffordable, workers may move farther from their workplaces, making longer commutes more common._\n\n3.          _This is particularly important because people without home internet access may otherwise struggle to complete online forms or study._\n\n4.          _Automated feedback should complement rather than replace teacher guidance, particularly for complex writing tasks._\n\n5.          _On balance, the benefits of wider access to learning outweigh the drawbacks, especially for students who have few local alternatives._\n\n## Key E15 — Error diagnosis and repairs\n\n|**Ex.**|**Primary error(s)**|**A more developed correction**|\n|---|---|---|\n|A|3, 4, 17, 20|_Digital learning tools can widen access to specialist lessons, especially for students in remote areas._|\n|B|13/16, grammar form|_Students can use AI to find information, but they should check whether the answers are accurate._|\n|C|4, 5|_Reliable public transport can reduce commuting costs because passengers do not need to pay for fuel or parking._|\n|D|9, 20|_Cities could reduce car dependence by improving public transport rather than relying on a complete ban on private vehicles._|\n|E|5, 8|_Demanding workloads can create stress when employees have little control over deadlines or working hours._|\n\n## Key E16 — 12 mini-task models (plans, not fixed answers)\n\n|**Mini task**|**Chosen position / focus**|**Argument 1: WHAT → WHY/HOW → RESULT**|**Argument 2: WHAT → WHY/HOW → RESULT**|**Suggested thesis / two topic sentences**|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|**16.1 Money management**|Agree|Budgeting: students learn to allocate income → fewer basic mistakes|Credit: understand interest/borrowing → more cautious choices|_I support compulsory financial literacy because it prepares students for everyday budgeting and borrowing decisions._ B1 budgeting; B2 borrowing|\n|**16.2 Environment**|Largely disagree that individuals have main responsibility|Individuals reduce waste → collective small benefits|Governments set standards/build infrastructure → enable change at scale|_Although individuals can reduce waste, governments should carry greater responsibility because they control major systems and regulations._ B1 individual role; B2 systemic reach|\n|**16.3 Group vs solo**|Discuss both, no required opinion|Group: explain ideas to peers → communication/feedback|Solo: own pace/accountability → independent focus|_Group projects encourage collaboration, whereas individual assignments can strengthen independent learning._ B1 group; B2 solo|\n|**16.4 Early languages**|Favor primary with suitable teaching|Secondary: more mature study skills → structured learning|Primary: frequent low-pressure exposure → confidence with sounds/communication|_Although older students may study languages more systematically, I favour an earlier start because regular exposure can build confidence._ B1 secondary; B2 primary+opinion|\n|**16.5 Online degrees**|Describe both, no weigh|Flexible access → working adults can study|Limited practical contact → harder for hands-on courses|_Online degrees offer accessibility but can restrict face-to-face and practical learning._ B1 access; B2 practical constraints|\n|**16.6 Four-day week**|Benefits outweigh in suitable sectors|Challenge: customer-service coverage → shift planning required|Better recovery + focused hours → well-being without necessary loss of output|_Where staffing can be managed effectively, the well-being benefits of a four-day week outweigh its scheduling challenges._ B1 staffing; B2 recovery + condition|\n|**16.7 Affordable housing**|Problem → matched solution|High rents → households move far away → long commutes|Affordable housing near jobs + planning reform → closer accommodation|_The shortage of affordable housing forces residents farther from work, so increasing supply in accessible areas should be a priority._ B1 impact; B2 response|\n|**16.8 Falling exercise**|Causes + targeted solutions|Desk jobs/time pressure → little daily movement|Workplaces/cities create active opportunities → easier daily exercise|_Sedentary routines and limited time contribute to inactivity; accessible exercise facilities and active travel options could help._ B1 causes; B2 solutions|\n|**16.9 Fewer children**|Cause/effect only|Housing/childcare expenses → delayed family planning|Smaller young cohorts → ageing workforce over time|_Rising living costs may discourage larger families, contributing over time to a greater share of older people in the population._ B1 causes; B2 effects|\n|**16.10 Reviews**|Common but trust cautiously|Buyers lack direct product experience → read reviews for reassurance|Manipulated/biased reviews → cross-check multiple sources|_Online reviews are popular because they reduce uncertainty, but consumers should verify them rather than trust every rating._ B1 reason; B2 trust judgement|\n|**16.11 Digital payments**|Positive with inclusion safeguards|Quick checkout/records → convenience|Some groups lack access → keep cash alternatives|_Digital payments are positive overall provided that cash remains available for people who cannot easily use digital services._ B1 benefits; B2 risk + condition|\n|**16.12 Car preference**|Causes + support measures discouraging use **with alternatives**|Poor bus frequency → cars seem more reliable|Improve transit + parking policy → practical shift|_People often choose cars because public transport is unreliable, and governments should discourage unnecessary driving only while improving alternatives._ B1 cause; B2 policy judgement|\n\n**Mini-task paragraph models — one worked example for 16.6:** _A shorter working week can improve employees’ well-being by giving them more time to recover between periods of work. When staff have sufficient rest, they may be better able to concentrate during working hours rather than spending long periods feeling exhausted. This could be particularly valuable in office-based roles where productivity depends on the quality of work rather than the number of hours spent at a desk. However, employers would still need to organise coverage carefully in industries that operate throughout the week._\n\n**For all E16 tasks:** Học viên cần tự viết một body paragraph từ chain trong bảng. Giáo viên không nên chấm thiếu một “đúng đáp án” duy nhất nếu argument khác hợp lý và trả lời đúng đề.\n\n## Key E17 — Complete worked application\n\n### Stage 1: Analyse\n\n•           **Topic:** AI tools in school education.\n\n•           **Task:** Discuss both views + give own opinion.\n\n•           **Scope:** Whether AI should be _taught or banned in classrooms_, not regulation of AI in society generally.\n\n•           **Position:** Schools should teach supervised, responsible use instead of imposing a complete ban.\n\n### Stages 2–3: Brainstorm → select\n\n**Possible ideas:** (1) easy cheating; (2) weaker independent thinking; (3) personalised feedback; (4) digital literacy; (5) teachers’ workload; (6) unequal access.  \n**Select:** View BAN = dishonest completion and dependence (related but manageable as one chain). View TEACH = learn to question and check AI output (clear mechanism and direct response).  \n**Remove for this essay:** “AI will change all future jobs” (too broad); “AI is exciting” (not an argument); “AI might replace every teacher” (not justified and outside the classroom policy focus).\n\n### Stage 4: Two argument chains\n\n|**Step**|**View 1 — ban**|**View 2 — teach responsibly**|\n|---|---|---|\n|WHAT|Bans may reduce misuse during assessed work|Guided AI use can build digital judgement|\n|WHY|Instant responses make copying easier|Students will encounter AI beyond school|\n|HOW|Learners submit generated work without checking it|Teachers require comparison, fact-checking and explanation|\n|RESULT|Harder to assess genuine ability|Students practise detecting errors and explaining choices|\n|EXAMPLE|Learner submits AI-generated essay they cannot defend|Student checks an AI-generated summary against course notes|\n|WHY IT MATTERS|Assessment needs to reflect authentic learning|Safe use supports learning and responsible future behaviour|\n\n### Stages 5–10: Thesis and paragraph map\n\n**Thesis:** _Although restricting AI can help protect academic integrity, I believe schools should teach students to use these tools responsibly instead of banning them completely._  \n**Body 1 topic sentence:** _Supporters of a ban are concerned that AI can make cheating and over-reliance easier._  \n**Body 2 topic sentence:** _However, guided use may be more beneficial because students need to learn how to judge AI-generated information._  \n**Introduction function:** define debate + state opinion; **Conclusion function:** weigh concerns and choose supervised teaching.\n\n### Stage 11: Full model essay — approximately 270–290 words\n\n_As artificial intelligence becomes more widely available, schools must decide how to respond to its use in classrooms. While some people support banning these tools to protect learning, I believe students should be taught to use them responsibly under teacher supervision._\n\n_Those who favour a ban argue that AI makes it easier for students to complete assignments without developing the necessary skills. For instance, a learner could submit an AI-generated essay without understanding its main arguments or checking whether the information is accurate. If this becomes common, teachers may find it difficult to distinguish genuine progress from work completed by a computer. Supporters therefore see restrictions as a way to protect academic honesty and encourage independent thinking. These concerns are particularly relevant when assignments are intended to measure what students can do on their own._\n\n_However, teaching responsible AI use may provide a more lasting solution. Since students are likely to encounter these tools outside school, simply banning them would leave an important skill untaught. Teachers could, for example, ask students to compare AI-generated explanations with reliable course materials and identify factual errors or weak reasoning. Through this process, learners would practise questioning information rather than accepting it automatically. Clear rules could also require students to explain which tools they used and complete certain assessments independently. This approach would preserve opportunities for independent work while developing the judgement needed to use emerging technologies effectively._\n\n_In conclusion, although banning AI may reduce certain forms of cheating, I believe supervised instruction is preferable. It addresses the risks of misuse while helping students become more critical and responsible users of technology._\n\n**Why this works (not an official examiner band award):** TR — discusses both views and own opinion; CC — B1 ban rationale, B2 response with mechanism; LR — precise verbs (_distinguish, compare, identify, require_) rather than inflated vocabulary; GRA — controlled conditionals, relative structures, and accurate reference.\n\n### Stage 12: Teacher feedback prompt\n\n•           **Task Response:** Does Body 1 represent the banning view fairly? Does the essay evaluate rather than just list?\n\n•           **Coherence:** Underline the link _ban → academic integrity_ and _teach → fact-checking → judgement_.\n\n•           **Lexical Resource:** Check natural collocations: _academic honesty, independent thinking, factual errors, course materials, teacher supervision_.\n\n•           **Grammar:** Check modal strength: _could/may_ where impacts are uncertain; no absolute claims.\n\n•           **One high-value revision:** Ask the student to replace one vague phrase (_AI is useful_) with an explicit **HOW** sentence.\n\n## Teacher’s final assessment routine (5 minutes per essay)\n\n1.          Circle the exact task verbs in the question; tick where the essay answers each one.\n\n2.          Box the thesis and underline the sentence in each body that directly supports it.\n\n3.          Draw arrows over the WHY → HOW → RESULT transitions; mark any missing link.\n\n4.          Select **only two** language errors to correct first: one recurring grammar issue, one imprecise collocation.\n\n5.          Return one actionable comment: _“Your position is clear; develop the second paragraph by explaining how the proposed rule would change student behaviour.”_\n\n**Official preparation sources (for task rules and marking framework):**  \nIELTS — Academic Writing test format: https://ielts.org/take-a-test/test-types/ielts-academic-test/ielts-academic-format-writing  \nIELTS — Writing test preparation resources: https://ielts.org/take-a-test/preparation-resources/writing-test-resources  \nIELTS — Writing band descriptors: https://ielts.org/cdn/ielts-guides/ielts-writing-band-descriptors.pdf\n\n**End of Workbook.**",
